    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to introduce 52 Mayeston Crescent to the market. This superb first floor two bedroom, two bathroom apartment comes to the market in excellent condition throughout, having been exceptionally well maintained by its current owner. Offering bright and spacious accommodation, together with a highly efficient B energy rating, this impressive property is sure to appeal to a wide range of buyers.\n\nThe property further benefits from ample parking and an exceptionally convenient location, close to a wealth of local amenities and excellent transport links.\n\nThe accommodation extends to approximately 66 sqm and briefly comprises a welcoming entrance hall with generous storage space, a bright and spacious open-plan kitchen/living/dining room filled with natural light, and access to a private patio overlooking a large communal green space.\n\nThere are two generous double bedrooms, both featuring fitted wardrobes. The main bedroom benefits an ensuite bathroom, while a large family bathroom completes the accommodation.\n\nMayeston Crescent enjoys a highly convenient location, with an abundance of amenities close by. Residents are within easy reach of numerous shops, Charlestown Shopping Centre, a range of sporting and leisure facilities, parks and excellent educational facilities, with Dublin City University (DCU) also nearby.\n\nThe property is ideally positioned for access to both Dublin Airport and Dublin City Centre, with numerous Dublin Bus routes providing excellent connectivity to destinations throughout the city. The M50 and M1 motorways are also just a short drive away, making this an ideal choice for commuters.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the quality, space and excellent location this superb apartment has to offer.\n\nLocal DNG agents: Isabel O'Neill, Ciaran Jones, Vincent Mullen, Michelle Keeley, Leah Barry & Brian McGee MIPAV.\n\nPlease Note: Some images have been digitally staged using AI to illustrate the potential of the property and its furnishings. These are for illustrative purposes only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nInviting entrance hallway with laminate wood flooring, tasteful painted décor and useful storage space.\n\nKitchen/Living/Dining Room - \nThis bright and spacious open plan kitchen, living and dining area features laminate wood flooring and tasteful painted décor. The kitchen is fitted with a range of cream high gloss wall and floor units, providing ample storage and workspace, while a separate storage cupboard houses the gas boiler. French doors open onto a private balcony, enjoying a pleasant outlook over the large open green space.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nGenerous double bedroom with laminate wood flooring, painted décor and built in fitted wardrobes. The room further benefits from access to a private ensuite bathroom.\n\nEn suite - \nThe ensuite bathroom features lino flooring, a wc, wash hand basin and shower cubicle.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nDouble bedroom with laminate wood flooring, painted décor and built in fitted wardrobes, providing excellent storage space.\n\nBathroom - \nThe main bathroom features lino flooring, wc wash hand basin and a bath with telephone shower. The walls are partially tiled with painted décor.\n\nBalcony - \nThe property enjoys a pleasant outlook overlooking the beautifully maintained communal gardens and playground area, providing a lovely green aspect and an attractive setting.\n\nExternally - \nThe property benefits from secure underground parking, with designated spaces and convenient access to the communal bin storage area. The development is surrounded by extensive green spaces and beautifully maintained communal grounds, creating a pleasant and peaceful setting for residents.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Year of construction 2007</li><li> Management fee: 1500 circa per annum</li><li> Excellent condition throughout</li><li> B Energy rating</li><li> 2 designated carpark spaces and visitor space available</li><li> Situated opposite a large green</li><li> Stylish fully fitted kitchen</li><li> Upvc Double glazed windows</li><li> Gas Fired Radiator Central heating</li><li> Walking distance to Charlestown Shopping Centre and Finglas Village</li><li> Close to Dublin Airport, DCU, M50 and City Centre</ul>"
      },
